    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "The names",
      "body": "Every Greek text, whether Plato or Xenophon or the New Testament, is full of proper names: people, places, gods. You cannot read Greek without reading these names, and you cannot read them without putting into practice everything you have learned in the first five lessons.\n\nToday you will read fifty names. Some will be familiar from English: Socrates, Plato, Athens. Others will be new. All are spelled in Greek as the Greeks spelled them. Read each one aloud before moving to the next. Do not rush. The goal is not speed but accuracy and confidence."
